post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'
MăngRS no longer needs the `input` group: /dev/uinput is handed to the
logged-in user by a session ACL (udev rule uaccess), so no account has to be
able to read /dev/input/event* for the engine to inject keys.

If you still belong to `input` (older install), remove it:
    sudo gpasswd -d "$USER" input
Log out and back in afterwards. The group can read every keystroke of the
machine, so keep it only if another tool of yours needs raw input access.

A leftover /etc/udev/rules.d/80-uinput.rules overrides the packaged rule.
Remove it so the session ACL applies:
    sudo rm /etc/udev/rules.d/80-uinput.rules
    sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}
